% The work of a rule whose literals after the first bind nothing it reads.
% Each p(_, X) after the first has X bound and `_` in its other column, so
% it tests whether p holds a tuple for X and lets the binding through once:
% the rule derives s(x) once for each of the two tuples the first literal
% scans, and the query once more.  stats-no-exists.dl runs the same program
% with the literals planned as lookups, each continuing the join once per
% tuple it matches.  The query is answered from the whole fixed point,
% without the Magic rewrite, so that the counts are the program's.

p(a, x).
p(b, x).

s(X) :- p(_, X), p(_, X), p(_, X).

s(X)?
